\f1\b0 \cf0 This directory is composed of two scripts that need to run simultaneously to properly acquire data. The 
\f0\b multi_servo_angle_node_new.py
\f1\b0  file creates a publisher node that will collect data from the 
\f0\b servo-back-and-forth-new.ino
\f1\b0  script and then publish it as a topic for subscriber nodes to pick up information. \
\
ROS2 will be needed to run the following codes. To install ROS2, please refer to ROS2 Tutorial in the Appendix. The tutorial is straightforward and easy to follow.\
\
\

\f2\i\b \ul Set-Up\

\f1\i0\b0 \ulnone You will need to open a minimum of two independent command windows to properly acquire data. A third window can be opened to check if the data is correctly uploaded by looking at the data on the topic:\

\f2\i\b \ul \

\f0\i0 \ulnone multi_servo_angle_node_new.py
\f2\i \ul :\ulnone  \

\f1\i0\b0 Call the node by typing the following command: \
$ run ros2 multi_servo_angle_node_new.py \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 multi_servo_angle_node_new\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \outl0\strokewidth0 multi_servo_angle_node_new is the name of the node.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb1 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 multi_servo_angle_node_new.py is the name of the package.\
\
\

\f0\b Servo-back-and-forth-new.ino:
\f1\b0 \
Upload the script to the Arduino board.\
\

\f0\b Third Window: \

\f1\b0 First, find the types of topic present in your system by typing:\
$ ros2 topic list\
\
Check if the topic where your data is being uploaded is present and run:\
$ ros2 topic info /name_of_the_topic\
\
This will allow you to check-in real time the angle data being processed by the Arduino. \
\
\

\f2\i\b \cf2 \ul \ulc2 Importance:
\f1\i0\b0 \cf0 \ulnone \
This directory is important as it is necessary to keep track of the the angular position of the sensors to properly estimate the position of the source and the central position of the submarine itself. \
\

\f2\i\b \ul Further Details:
\f1\i0\b0 \ulnone \
The servo-back-and-forth-new.ino script is home to an oscillating function that will move the sensors around while also tracking their angular positions.\
Notice that the servo-back-and-forth-new.ino script is not in python but in Arduino Language as the servos are directly controlled by an Arduino Controller. Thus, when modifying servo-back-and-forth-new.ino, make sure to employ the appropriate language. \
\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\

\f3\i Update Node:
\f1\i0 \
When editing the package of the node, make sure to update the package and its source.\
You can employ:\
$ colcon build --symlink-install       <\'97 this line will only need to be run once. This updates the package without needing to build it every time you modify it. \
$ source ~/.bashrc                         <\'97 this line will need to be run each time you update the package.\
For further help, please refer to:\
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wfCuPQ_6VbI&list=PLLSegLrePWgJudpPUof4-nVFHGkB62Izy&index=5 \
\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\
Any other details about the code can be found in the scripts themselves. \
